WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.170
Michael Bay's first Transformers movie turned
Megan Fox into an instant star.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.370
Men's magazines couldn't get enough of her,
and her future in Hollywood seemed all but

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.370
bulletproof.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:16.449
Who knew that a mere decade later, Fox would
still be playing second fiddle to CGI creations?

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:21.289
Outside of the running-on-fumes Teenage Mutant
Ninja Turtles franchise, her box office prospects

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:22.750
have been pretty dire of late.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.279
"I am still socially relevant."

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:29.789
Here's why Hollywood won't cast Megan Fox
anymore.

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:31.189
Transformer trouble

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:35.149
You'd think an actress would stay faithful
to the franchise that launched her stardom,

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:39.280
but there's been some bad blood between Megan
Fox and the crew of Transformers.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.790
When Michael Bay cast Megan Fox in 2007's
toy-centric blockbuster, she was still mostly

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.859
unknown outside of a few small TV roles.

00:00:47.859 --> 00:00:53.649
By the time Transformers: Revenge of the Fallen
rolled out in 2009, Fox was a mega-star...who

00:00:53.649 --> 00:00:56.710
had a few mega problems with her starring
vehicle.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.501
Fox took shots at the effects-heavy Revenge,
telling Entertainment Weekly, "People are

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.960
well aware that this is not a movie about
acting."

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.060
But even that comment was tame compared to
the way she described Michael Bay: "He wants

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.430
to be like Hitler on his sets, and he is."

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.430
Whoops!

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.540
Comparing your boss to history's most infamous
genocidal dictator isn't going to fly in most

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.560
workplaces.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.280
Bay told GQ that while Fox was part of the
rehearsal process for Transformers: Dark of

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.760
the Moon early on, she was dropped before
filming began.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.960
Bay recalled, "[Fox] was in a different world,
on her BlackBerry.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.570
You gotta stay focused.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.180
And you know, the Hitler thing.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.710
Steven [Spielberg] said, 'Fire her right now.'"

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:44.740
Dark of the Moon screenwriter Ehren Kruger
echoed that sentiment, saying that Fox "seemed

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.240
like an actress who didn't want to be a part
of it.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:50.909
She was saying she wanted to, but she wasn't
acting like it."

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:52.939
Flop fest

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:57.329
Transformers may have raked in truckloads
of cash, but Megan Fox's three follow-up films

00:01:57.329 --> 00:01:59.760
crashed and burned spectacularly.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:04.520
First was 2009's Jennifer's Body, a low budget
horror thriller that attempted to build off

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.220
Fox's growing star power by putting her front
and center in the marketing campaign.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.490
But reviews were mixed, and the R-rated film
earned a mere $6.8 million on its opening

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.490
weekend.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:20.850
Then, Fox appeared in 2010's Jonah Hex, a
critical and box office disaster.

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:26.270
She now openly admits that Jonah Hex was a
turkey, saying in 2016 that "no one should

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.650
ever see that movie."

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:33.380
The same year, Fox made a stab for indie cred
with Passion Play, a 2010 drama starring Mickey

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.020
Rourke, Bill Murray, and Rhys Ifans.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:41.180
Despite the all-star cast, the film was critically
reviled and only played in a handful of theaters

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.480
before being dumped to DVD.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.030
Even Mickey Rourke slammed it, dubbing it
"another terrible movie" on his resume.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:52.050
And Mickey Rourke knows a few things about
terrible movies.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.900
Overexposed

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:58.180
Around the time of the one-two career sucker
punch of Revenge of the Fallen and Jennifer's

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.980
Body, the Megan Fox backlash began.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.100
The combination of the massive marketing for
her movies and her appearance on every late

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:10.400
night talk show, magazine, and online photo
gallery caused serious Fox fatigue.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:17.430
"Megan Fox Media Oversaturation syndrome is
a neurobiological disorder stemming from oversaturation

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.140
of Megan Fox related media"

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:25.190
It got so bad, several men's websites actually
called for "A Day Without Megan Fox" boycott.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:30.470
When even AskMen.com is tired of seeing Fox
in various states of undress, something is

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:31.580
definitely off.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:36.000
"This would be a perfect moment, except you
landed on my testicles."

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.920
False starts

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.920
Fox has been linked to a number of would-be
franchises over the years, including a film

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.450
version of the '90s "bad girl" comic Fathom,
which revolves around aquatic heroine Aspen.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.330
But the project stalled, with Fox admitting
in 2014 that she may be getting too old to

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.330
play the twenty-something character.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:58.790
And with so much of the film set underwater,
"unless James Cameron is going to direct it

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.140
I don't know how we're going to make it happen."

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.960
And seriously, if you're looking to get past
your sex icon typecasting, this probably isn't

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.430
the role to make it happen.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:08.540
Jane Eyre, maybe.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.060
Or Lady Wolfman.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.790
But...not Aspen.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:17.260
Fox did return to blockbuster filmmaking as
April O'Neil in the 2014 Teenage Mutant Ninja

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.260
Turtles reboot.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:22.700
But after the sequel, Teenage Mutant Ninja
Turtles: Out of the Shadows, grossed half

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:27.480
of what its predecessor made, the third installment
may never make it out of its shell, marking

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.400
yet another failed franchise in the Fox filmography.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.410
A comedic return

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.900
Fox has found success in recent years by taking
supporting roles in comedies where she can

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.370
tweak her aloof, glamorous image.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:45.040
She showed off her comedic side with turns
in This Is 40 and The Dictator, and joined

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:50.600
New Girl as a regular cast member in 2016
while star Zooey Deschanel was on maternity

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.600
leave.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.940
Meanwhile, her role in the James Franco period
comedy Zeroville proves that there's life

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.770
after Bay for Megan Fox.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:02.250
If she keeps working in roles like these,
Megan Fox may still have a long career in

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:03.850
Hollywood ahead of her.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:04.850
And hey!

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:09.150
If acting jobs dry up, Fox can always try
working as a studio executive:

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:13.690
"I am going to eat your soul."

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:14.690
See?

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:15.690
She's a natural!

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:16.930
Thanks for watching!

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:20.040
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.590
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

